# Generated from: specs/214-replace-markdown-steering-with-a-managed-runtime-sdlc-steering-and-deterministic-verification/requirements.md
Feature: Managed steering runtime and deterministic verification
  As a developer on a managed nmg-sdlc project
  I want a versioned steering runtime, project snippets, and deterministic validations
  So that required checks are enforced by core code and guidance reaches prompts through one registry path

  # --- Happy Path ---

  @SCN001
  Scenario: steering command plans and applies a valid runtime
    Given a managed repository and a natural-language steering prompt
    When /sdlc-steering runs in native plan mode and its exact plan is approved
    Then the shared writer creates or updates the manifest, fixed modules, and declared project files
    And it validates the complete staged runtime before replacing live files
    And headless invocation fails closed with the TUI-only message

  @SCN002
  Scenario: approved upgrade removes legacy dual authority safely
    Given legacy product, tech, and structure steering documents
    When the steering-runtime upgrade category is approved
    Then the writer migrates their project content into registered snippets
    And it removes the legacy documents only after staged validation succeeds
    And unknown files, snippets, extensions, and retrospective are preserved

  @SCN003
  Scenario: onboard delegates to the shared writer
    Given greenfield or enhancement onboarding needs steering
    When the approved onboard plan applies
    Then onboard initializes the same manifest and managed modules
    And it does not create legacy steering documents as live authorities

  @SCN004
  Scenario: every applicable required validation fails closed
    Given schema-valid validations with closed when conditions
    When verify-code verifies the issue
    Then core evaluates each condition before provider launch
    And every applicable required validation runs with identity-bound evidence
    And any required non-pass forbids Pass and PR Evidence Pending

  # --- Alternative Paths ---

  @SCN005
  Scenario Outline: core owns applicability
    Given a required validation whose core-evaluated condition is <condition>
    When the provider phase is reached
    Then the provider is <launch>
    And the effective result is <result>

    Examples:
      | condition | launch | result |
      | false | not launched | skipped by core |
      | true and provider returns passed evidence | launched | passed |
      | true and provider returns skipped | launched | incomplete |
      | true and provider returns not_applicable | launched | incomplete |

  # --- Error Handling ---

  @SCN006
  Scenario Outline: invalid registration fails closed
    Given a steering runtime with <fault>
    When steering validation or verify discovery runs
    Then it fails with <reasonCode>
    And no partial runtime or validation set is accepted

    Examples:
      | fault | reasonCode |
      | an unknown manifest key | steering_manifest_unknown_key |
      | a duplicate registration id | steering_duplicate_id |
      | a path escaping steering | steering_path_outside_root |
      | an invalid fixed module set | steering_module_invalid |
      | an unresolved provider | steering_provider_unresolved |
      | an invalid when condition | steering_condition_invalid |
      | stale provider evidence | steering_evidence_stale |

  # --- Edge Cases ---

  @SCN007
  Scenario: project snippets use the registry without result authority
    Given registered project snippets with allowed consumers and slots
    When a matching command or worker prompt renders
    Then the prompt registry inserts them in declared order with provenance
    And undeclared project files are not scanned
    And snippet prose cannot mutate or raise a core validation result
